('R02-00206','02_repeated_release','production','crypto/evp/m_sigver.c','do_sigver_init','84;277','INCONCLUSIVE','Medium','At line 84, !reinit calls evp_pkey_ctx_free_old_ops(locpctx). The old operation is not replaced until lines 187-189. If provider-key export fails, the provkey == NULL path at 176-180 reaches err and calls the helper again at 277 before setting operation undefined. The helper’s GEN branch at crypto/evp/pmeth_lib.c:228-232 dispatches gen_cleanup but does not clear ctx->op.keymgmt.genctx; the DH cleanup at providers/implementations/keymgmt/dh_kmgmt.c:865-874 frees that context. A non-NULL pkey with an active generation context can be formed by the documented EVP_PKEY_CTX_new_from_pkey + EVP_PKEY_keygen_init path and assigned to EVP_MD_CTX via EVP_MD_CTX_set_pkey_ctx. However, the default unsupported-DH path is routed through notsupported; I did not establish a valid provider/key state that reaches provkey == NULL while the old generation context remains live.','Source-level cleanup hazard identified; exact feasible provider failure path and runtime impact remain unconfirmed. No runtime reproduction.'),
('R02-00204','02_repeated_release','production','crypto/evp/m_sigver.c','do_sigver_init','135;267;279;284','FP','High','The loop frees tmp_keymgmt at line 135 and immediately sets it to NULL at line 136 before any reassignment. Later cleanup calls at lines 267, 279, and 284 are mutually exclusive success/error/not-supported exits, not multiple releases on one path. The historical fix-register entry for this same function concerned stale signature/tmp_keymgmt values between loop iterations; the pinned source visibly contains the pointer resets.','Source-level review only; this is a heuristic classification, not runtime validation. Same function appears in historical fix register, so this is retrospective context.'),
