('R02-00072','02_repeated_release','production_or_application','apps/s_client.c','psk_use_session_cb','240;249;252','FP','High','The free at line 240 is in the cipher == NULL branch and returns immediately. The free at line 249 is in the session-setup failure branch and jumps to err. The free at line 252 is only on successful setup. These branches cannot release the same key allocation twice.','Source-level review only; no runtime reproduction.'),
('R02-00301','02_repeated_release','production','crypto/store/store_meth.c','OSSL_STORE_LOADER_free','59;62','FP','High','The two free_loader calls are in mutually exclusive #ifdef OPENSSL_NO_CACHED_FETCH and #else branches. Only one branch is compiled into a translation unit. This candidate was outside the first 430-file lexical prefilter and was found by the optimized whole-tree pass.','Source-level review only; no runtime reproduction.'),
('R02-00318','02_repeated_release','production','crypto/ui/ui_lib.c','general_allocate_boolean','183;186','FP','High','free_string(s) at line 183 is the failed stack-push branch; line 186 is the mutually exclusive allocate_string_stack failure branch. The conditional structure permits only one release.','Source-level review only; no runtime reproduction.'),
('R02-00319','02_repeated_release','production','crypto/ui/ui_lib.c','general_allocate_string','137;140','FP','High','free_string(s) at line 137 is the failed stack-push branch; line 140 is the mutually exclusive allocate_string_stack failure branch. The conditional structure permits only one release.','Source-level review only; no runtime reproduction.'),
('R02-00101','02_repeated_release','production','crypto/asn1/f_string.c','a2i_ASN1_STRING','95;102;113;132','FP','High','The frees at lines 95, 102, and 113 each immediately return from the function. Line 132 is the shared err cleanup reached from other parse failures, not after those free-and-return branches. This same function was independently triaged as a Clang null-dereference FP; the Coccinelle repeated-release pattern is a separate syntactic signal.','Source-level review only; do not treat the shared function match as a second defect.'),
